# THE SURVIVOR BASELINE. One line per mutant `avra attack`'s malformed
# class ACCEPTS: <feature><TAB><source><TAB><reason>. A survivor is not
# a failure — it may be a VALID program — so the tolerance law stays and
# this records the accepted set: a NEW survivor is refused, and an entry
# that now REFUSES is stale. The baseline lists sites, never counts.
grammar_lit	{ "s" }	valid mutant: `{ "s" }` is a BLOCK — deleting `grammar` leaves a valid program
impls	trait x { \n \n }	valid mutant: an empty `trait` declaration
impls	trait x { \n \n } \n	valid mutant: an empty trait declaration and a blank line
impls	trait x { \n }	valid mutant: an empty trait declaration
impls	trait x { \n } \n \n	valid mutant: an empty trait declaration
impls	trait x { } \n \n	valid mutant: an empty trait declaration
maps	\n { }	valid mutant: an empty map literal
maps	{ \n \n }	valid mutant: an empty map literal
maps	{ }	valid mutant: an empty map literal
maps	{ } \n	valid mutant: an empty map literal
